@startuml j3-quick-entry-voice
title J3 Quick entry: speak or type "Sunita 500 udhaar", the form fills, the owner saves
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundCorner 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam titleFontSize 17
skinparam titleFontColor #0E5C45
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #0E5C45
  LifeLineBorderColor #7FA89A
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #E8F2EE
  ParticipantBorderColor #0E5C45
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F2EE
  ParticipantFontColor #0B3D2E
  ActorBorderColor #0E5C45
  ActorBackgroundColor #E8F2EE
  ActorFontColor #0B3D2E
  GroupBorderColor #0E5C45
  GroupHeaderFontColor #0E5C45
  GroupBackgroundColor #F3F8F6
  DividerBorderColor #0E5C45
  DividerBackgroundColor #E8F2EE
  DividerFontColor #0B3D2E
  BoxBorderColor #0E5C45
}
skinparam database {
  BorderColor #0E5C45
  BackgroundColor #E8F2EE
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #B08A2E
  BackgroundColor #FFF8E6
  FontSize 12
}
actor "Shop owner" as Owner
participant "Browser UI\n(index.html)" as UI
participant "app.js" as App
participant "Web Speech API\n(browser)" as SR
autonumber
note over UI, App : setupVoice() at init: the mic button (#quick-mic) is shown only when\nSpeechRecognition or webkitSpeechRecognition exists; otherwise only typing
alt voice path
  Owner -> UI : tap the mic
  UI -> App : click handler
  App -> SR : new SpeechRecognition(); lang = hi-IN, te-IN or en-IN by app language;\ninterim results on, one phrase; start()
  App -> UI : #quick-msg "Listening..."; mic aria-pressed = true
  Owner -> SR : speak, for example "Sunita 500 udhaar" or "सुनीता 500 उधार"
  SR -> App : onresult: transcript
  App -> UI : write the transcript into #quick-input
  opt owner taps the mic again
    App -> SR : stop()
  end
  alt onerror
    SR -> App : error
    App -> UI : no-speech: "Did not catch that..."\nnot-allowed: "The microphone is blocked..."\naudio-capture: "No microphone was found..."\nnetwork: "This browser's speech service did not answer..."\nother: "Could not use the microphone..."
    note right of App : language-not-supported: tried once more in en-IN
  else onend with words heard
    SR -> App : onend
    App -> App : onQuick()
  else v1.2.4: onend with no words and no error
    SR -> App : onend
    App -> UI : "Did not catch that. Try again or type it."
  else nothing for 9 seconds
    App -> SR : abort()
    App -> UI : "This browser's speech service did not answer..."
  end
  note right of App
    v1.2.4: every failure line is followed by a tip.
    Phone or tablet (user agent Android, iPhone, iPad, iPod):
    quickKeyTip, the microphone key of the keyboard.
    Anything else, a touch-screen laptop too:
    quickPcTip, Windows key and H (on a Mac, the microphone key).
  end note
else typed path
  Owner -> UI : type in #quick-input, press Enter or the Fill button
  UI -> App : submit: onQuick()
end
App -> App : parseQuick(text)
note right of App : v1.2: in the nine languages from langs.js, that language's\ncredit and payment words are taught to the parser (H.quickWords)
note right of App
  Hindi and Telugu digits become 0-9; ₹ and Rs dropped; 1,500 and 5k read as numbers
  first number = amount; hazaar, sau, lakh, thousand, hundred multiply it
  payment words (paid, jama, mila, upi, gpay...) win over credit words (udhaar, diya, baki...)
  name score per customer: exact word 3, prefix 2, one letter off 1,
  full phone 10, last four digits 4; English, Hindi and Telugu forms of each name
  words that are not names go to the note
end note
App -> App : applyQuick(p, the open customer, or none on the overview)
alt several customers tie for the best score
  App -> UI : "More than one customer matches. Pick one:" with up to 6 buttons
  Owner -> UI : tap one
  UI -> App : applyQuick(p, chosen customer)
else no customer matches
  App -> UI : "Which customer? Say the name..."
else customer found, no amount above zero
  App -> UI : select the customer; "Say or type an amount..."; focus Amount
else customer and amount found
  App -> UI : set type (credit when no type word), amount, date if empty, note
  App -> UI : "Filled: {name}, {type} {amt}. Check it, then press Save entry."
  App -> UI : focus Save entry
  note right of UI : nothing is saved yet
  Owner -> UI : check the form, then press Save entry
  UI -> App : onEntrySubmit(), as in J2
end
@enduml
